  "scope_limits": [
    "This fixes a diagnostic classification gap demonstrated by the host fixture. All three prior receive-only native API-loss cases retained7; it is not claimed to have caused either older product restore refusal.",
    "The positive host fixture compiles the explicit PD_LAB_HOST_TEST identity bypass; the separate binary without that macro still rejects the ordinary host identity before files. No radio, socket or privilege-changing operation occurs in these tests.",
    "All ten host cases pass, including maximum pair/trace/fit bounds, no-idle discard, API7 with/without idle, generic error discard, foreign file, symlink file/directory, mode and production-identity refusals. They do not prove actual keyed native exit ordering or hardware unkey.",
    "The patch changes only the bench overlay header. Go, DSP mathematical code, ownership/restore/RF admission, source duration and fixed privileged helpers remain unchanged.",
    "ARMv7/ARM64 reproducibility, ordinary installation, exact receive-only validation and a separately prepared bounded keyed fault remain required before qualification. No production, actual6300 or full P1-P10 completion claim."
  ],
  "next_step": "Reproduce the exact API-exit-preserving diagnostic runtime for ARMv7/ARM64 with unchanged Go/fixed helpers, preserve complete source/artifacts and upgrade normally from aa56. Validate the exact new runtime receive-only first. Then separately prepare and dispatch one bounded keyed DSP API-loss case through the pinned GUI with independent unkey/power guards and explicit receive recovery, without RF retry/rearm or software reboot."
